  rooms: "Six rooms: two [ ] windows, two { } rooms and two < > passages; four kept by Boof, the rest by the berries and the echo."
  told_by: "Told by the narrator, Boof, the boonberries, an echo and the Fool."
  made_of: "Made most of steam and warmth, then boonberries, then oak and frame."
  wonders: "First met here: echo-wrens, the lag-stag, rehearsal moths and a saying, “Try it again, a little changed”."
  palette: "Its palette is the grove, earned a layer at a time: moss and leaf-dark green with a straw-pale light: the grove that answers a beat late."
  berries: "A boneberry in this chapter tastes of mushroom broth."
  harmonies: "Torch-ants will not settle where a light comes back twice. The berries remember the egg's hum. Warm roots keep the berries in their light. A boonberry foresees kindly. The egg rides against her ribs."
}

